    "captions": {
      "pone.0319031.g007": {
        "line": 515,
        "caption_text": "Boxplot representation for therNassoc(V1, V2, V) index distribution when: a) αwit=αbet=0.5, b) αwit=0.75, αbet=0.5, c) αwit=0.5, αbet=0.75 and d) αwit=αbet=0.75 for d=0.4. Each panel shows the boxplots describing the rNassoc(V1, V2, V) distribution as a function of the within/between cluster ratio ρ. The symbol * indicates a statistically significant result (i.e., p<0.05) for the post hoc Tuckey HSD test.",
        "figure_xref_targets": []
      },
      "pone.0319031.g008": {
        "line": 556,
        "caption_text": "Boxplot representation for therNcut(V1, V2) index distribution when: a) αwit=αbet=0.5, b) αwit=0.05, αbet=0.75, c) αwit=0.5, αbet=0.75 and d) αwit=αbet=0.75 for d=0.4. Each panel shows the boxplots describing the rNcut(V1, V2) distribution as a function of the within/between cluster ratio ρ. The symbol * indicates a statistically significant result (i.e., p<0.05) for the post hoc Tuckey HSD test.",
        "figure_xref_targets": []
      },
      "pone.0319031.t003": {
